Q4: is a tapered format reachable by intersecting the two named families?
    Intersection takes the canonical exponent pointwise maximum, so the
    reachable slopes are the maxima of the operands' slopes. Measured,
    not argued:
    slopes of the canonical exponent over every pairwise intersection: [0, 1]
    slopes of posit<8,0>'s canonical exponent: [0, 1, 2]
    slopes of posit<8,1>'s canonical exponent: [0, 1, 2]
    slopes of posit<10,2>'s canonical exponent: [0, 1, 2]

    A slope above one is not a maximum of slopes at most one, so a
    tapered format is not in the intersection-closure of the two
    named families, while it is in the general class (i1b).

